#
# THE DEMO BUILD'S VARIABLES. Read by `vite build --mode demo`.
#
# Exact command, and what it produces: docs/deploy/console-build.md.
#
# ── PHASE 1 IS THE DEFAULT, AND THAT IS THE POINT ────────────────────────────────
#
# docs/leads/deploy-plan.md §4: "Nobody is allowed to let the live path hold the URL
# hostage." So the file committed here builds the demo that CANNOT FAIL — a console over
# a cryptographically verified EvidenceBundle, no backend, no database in the request
# path. `VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE` is deliberately EMPTY, which `src/app/source-select.ts`
# treats as unset, so this build carries exactly one source and the badge reads REPLAY.
#
# Phase 2 adds the live API by supplying the variable in the ENVIRONMENT, which Vite
# applies after every .env file, so no committed file is edited by a deploy:
#
#     VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE=/ pnpm exec vite build --mode demo
#
# `/` and not a hostname: the console and the API are served from ONE CloudFront
# distribution (deploy-plan §2.1), so `/v1/...` resolves against whatever origin the page
# was loaded from. There is no CORS anywhere and the built artefact names no domain.
#
# With both set the console starts LIVE and shows a control that switches to REPLAY —
# the same screen, two sources, one badge that never lies about which one you are
# looking at.
#
# ── MEASURED 2026-08-14: WHAT EACH OF THE TWO COMMANDS ACTUALLY EMITS ────────────
#
# Three clean builds each, from a `git archive HEAD` export of this directory, recorded
# asset-by-asset with sha256 in `evidence/deploy/console-repro.json`. Both are byte
# identical across their three runs.
#
#   Phase 1  (this file alone)         assets/index-DzVoV1YM.js   433,564 B   REPLAY
#   Phase 2  (VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE=/) assets/index-CmIr4_KY.js   433,565 B   LIVE + switch
#
# ONE BYTE apart: `VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE:""` becomes `VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE:"/"`. The
# Phase-1 digest is byte-for-byte the object the deployed Function URL is serving today
# (`sha256 4596d00c…`, `web/assets/index-DzVoV1YM.js` in the Lambda package), so the
# artefact a judge reached is reproducible from this file and nothing else — and the
# console read REPLAY because the deploy ran the Phase-1 command, not because anything
# here was wrong.
#
# ⚠ THE HAZARD IS THE ARGUMENT, NOT ONLY THE ENV PREFIX. `docs/deploy/console-build.md`
# §1 records MSYS rewriting a bare `/` in `VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE=/ pnpm exec vite build`.
# It rewrites a bare `/` passed as ANY argument on a Git Bash line, before the process
# starts — measured again here on 2026-08-14, and the artefact compiled
# `VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE:"C:/Program Files/Git/"`, a path on somebody's laptop named by a
# page served on the internet. Use PowerShell (`$env:VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE='/'`) or
# `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`, and ALWAYS read the compiled literal back out of the bytes.
# `scripts/deploy/console_repro.py` refuses the converted value by name.

# ── The bundle (Phase 1 and Phase 2) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Relative on purpose. `vite.config.ts` sets `base: './'` so the console runs from a
# bucket root, from a sub-path and from `file://`; a bundle URL that named an origin
# would undo all three. `src/app/composition.tsx` resolves it against `document.baseURI`
# before the bundle player sees it, so it is always same-origin.
#
# The directory is produced by `w9-evidence-bundle` and uploaded beside `index.html`.
VITE_MAINLINE_BUNDLE_URL=./bundle/

# ── The live API (Phase 2 only) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Empty = unset = this build has no live source. Supply it in the environment, above.
VITE_MAINLINE_API_BASE=

# ── The verifier's trust anchor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `src/verify/config.ts`: with no key the checkpoint SIGNATURE check is a named SKIP, the
# seal is amber, and the honesty chrome says so. It is never green and never red, because
# a checkpoint nobody could check has not been accused of anything. File digests are
# still recomputed in the browser and a mismatch still refuses to render.
#
# Set it to the C2SP vkey of the log signing key — `<origin>+<8 hex id>+<base64 SPKI>` —
# when the custody domain publishes one. A malformed value is discarded rather than used.
VITE_MAINLINE_LOG_VKEY=

# SHA-256 of the canonicaliser source, pinned in spec/custody/canon-registry.yaml. With
# none, ledger check 10 SKIPs and says so.
VITE_MAINLINE_CANON_SHA256=
